{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","externalID":"s:19SegmentSpecEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV","symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"SegmentSpecEncoding"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder.swift#L90"}},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/init(plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true,"title":"Type Aliases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Type Properties"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one member, ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an array","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s session, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" when its context has no session"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event\/name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as it is","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"request_ip","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"track\""}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"code":"identify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call, no traits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no "},{"code":"context.device.id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"advertisingId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". An endpoint counts a user per "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call with neither a "},{"code":"userId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" nor an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Segment deduplicates calls by "},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over about the last 24 hours, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops most duplicates rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the app ended is most likely not stored again, whatever its "},{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". RudderStack’s and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":" member from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the request unless the call has one, even when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" is set, and passes it on to its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":". Customer.io’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"references don’t say whether "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"type":"text","text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"type":"text","text":", which their specs don’t have."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"originalTimestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"channel"},{"type":"text","text":" is sent. Without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" the endpoint takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sentAt"},{"type":"text","text":" would be the first attempt’s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the call."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"text":" reads them. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out, an element of an array is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the bundle identifier, "},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each left out when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; no "},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when all three are"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: "},{"code":"ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for a phone or pad, "},{"code":"macos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"tvos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"watchos","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"visionos","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"network"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wifi"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cellular"},{"text":", whether the connection is each","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sent: one whose event and version ","type":"text"},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name is one of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Customer.io’s semantic events, which delete or suppress people and devices, one whose event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and one too large for a call (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"text":"). ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" returns them as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" logs and reports on its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/SegmentSpecBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sends","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing for it. A record sent again keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"messageId","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The bytes are the same for the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records on every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"UTF-8 bytes.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol",